From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <herman@mailbox.org>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/conmakehash: don't embed the build path in output

Kbuild invokes this as "scripts/conmakehash $(src)/$(FONTMAPFILE)"; for
out-of-tree (O=) builds $(src) is $(srctree)/drivers/tty/vt, so argv[1]
is an absolute path containing ${WORKDIR}/${TMPDIR}. That path ends up
in the "automatically generated by" comment of consolemap_deftbl.c and
trips the "buildpaths" QA check on the -src package.

Strip the $srctree prefix (exported by the top-level Makefile) from the
input filename before printing it, same as upstream commit 2fca0fd71981
("tty: vt: conmakehash: Don't mention the full path of the input in
output") does with abs_srctree. This kernel predates both that move to
drivers/tty/vt/ and the abs_srctree export, so adapt the fix to
scripts/conmakehash.c and to the srctree variable this Makefile actually
exports.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.yoctoproject.org/linux-yocto/commit/?h=v5.15/standard/base&id=2fca0fd719812ea2ff67630b01355aa80481623e]
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <herman@mailbox.org>
---
 scripts/conmakehash.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/conmakehash.c b/scripts/conmakehash.c
index 1111111111111..2222222222222 100644
--- a/scripts/conmakehash.c
+++ b/scripts/conmakehash.c
@@ -80,6 +80,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 {
   FILE *ctbl;
   char *tblname;
+  char *rel_tblname;
   char buffer[65536];
   int fontlen;
   int i, nuni, nent;
@@ -104,6 +105,19 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 	}
     }
 
+  /* Strip $srctree from the input path so the generated file doesn't
+     embed the build path (Kbuild exports srctree as an absolute path
+     for O= builds). */
+  rel_tblname = tblname;
+  {
+    char *srctree = getenv("srctree");
+    size_t srctree_len = srctree ? strlen(srctree) : 0;
+
+    if (srctree_len && !strncmp(tblname, srctree, srctree_len) &&
+	tblname[srctree_len] == '/')
+      rel_tblname = tblname + srctree_len + 1;
+  }
+
   /* For now we assume the default font is always 256 characters. */
   fontlen = 256;
 
@@ -256,7 +270,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 #include <linux/types.h>\n\
 \n\
 u8 dfont_unicount[%d] = \n\
-{\n\t", argv[1], fontlen);
+{\n\t", rel_tblname, fontlen);
 
   for ( i = 0 ; i < fontlen ; i++ )
     {
-- 
